{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And the princes of Israel offered.</b> This is what it says immediately — 'and they brought their offering' etc." "<b>Who stood over the counting.</b> Rashi explained that they stood with Moses and Aaron when they counted Israel, as it is said 'and with you they shall be' etc. Therefore 'and they brought their offering' for atonement, because they counted Israel. And so we find in the section of Midian: 'your servants have taken [the head of] the men of war who were in our hand' etc., 'and let us bring HaShem's offering to atone for our souls.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:16:48.382692935Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}